## T2 · Key quotations

::: table | Quotations worth reproducing exactly.
@widths 4,10
@font 9.5
Speaker | Words
Bhasin and Khan (1986) | "An awareness of women's oppression and exploitation in society, at work and within the family, and conscious action by women and men to change this situation."
bell hooks (2000) | "Simply put, feminism is a movement to end sexism, sexist exploitation, and oppression."
Rebecca West (1913) | "People call me a feminist whenever I express sentiments that differentiate me from a doormat or a prostitute."
Seneca Falls (1848) | "All men and women are created equal."
J. S. Mill (1869) | "What is now called the nature of women is an eminently artificial thing."
Engels (1884) | "The world historical defeat of the female sex."
Federici (1975) | "They say it is love. We say it is unwaged work."
Freud (1924) | "Anatomy is destiny."
Juliet Mitchell (1974) | "Psychoanalysis is not a recommendation for a patriarchal society, but an analysis of one."
Redstockings (1969) | "Women are an oppressed class."
Lyotard (1979) | "Incredulity toward metanarratives."
Spivak (1988) | "White men are saving brown women from brown men."
Jinnah (1944) | "No nation can rise to the height of glory unless your women are side by side with you."
:::
